<!--
Optional Openbox window rules for the dedicated session set up by
openbox-autostart.example: they start EasyEffects and AudioRelay
minimized instead of popping their window on top of Chromium.

These go inside the <applications>...</applications> section of
~/.config/openbox/rc.xml, not in the autostart script - Openbox reads
window rules from rc.xml, not from autostart. If you don't have a
personal rc.xml yet, Openbox is using your distro's default one (on
Fedora, /etc/xdg/openbox/rc.xml); copy that to
~/.config/openbox/rc.xml first, then add the rules below inside its
existing <applications> block.

The class values below match what EasyEffects and AudioRelay actually
register (checked with `xprop WM_CLASS` while each was running) - they
aren't guessed from the package/app name.
-->

<application class="easyeffects">
  <iconic>yes</iconic>
</application>

<application class="com-azefsw-audioconnect-desktop-app-MainKt">
  <iconic>yes</iconic>
</application>
